- `AntitoneCertificate.monoOn`? trivial.

Consequences of `MonotoneCertificate`:
- `F_le_of_le`, `F_ge_at`, `upper_le_value` (`F t ≤ upperBound`), `eq_of_le_of_eq`.

These are the "algebraic consequences". To ensure at least two, we have many.

**(b) Continuous certificates over ℝ:**

```lean
structure ContinuousMonotoneCertificate {X} [MeasurableSpace X] {μ : Measure X}
    (E : ℝ → EntropyData X μ) : Type where
  dissipation : ℝ → ℝ
  hasDerivAt_F : ∀ t, 0 < t → HasDerivAt (fun s => F (E s)) (dissipation t) t
  continuousOn_F : ContinuousOn (fun s => F (E s)) (Set.Ici 0)
  dissipation_nonneg : ∀ t, 0 < t → 0 ≤ dissipation t
  upperBound : ℝ
  upper_le : ∀ t, 0 ≤ t → F (E t) ≤ upperBound
```

Theorem `monotoneOn_F`:
```lean
theorem ContinuousMonotoneCertificate.monotoneOn (c) :
    MonotoneOn (fun t => F (E t)) (Set.Ici 0) := by
  apply monotoneOn_of_deriv_nonneg (convex_Ici 0) c.continuousOn_F
  · intro x hx
    have hx' : 0 < x := by simpa [interior_Ici] using hx
    exact (c.hasDerivAt_F x hx').differentiableAt.differentiableWithinAt
  · intro x hx
    have hx' : 0 < x := by simpa [interior_Ici] using hx
    rw [(c.hasDerivAt_F x hx').deriv]
    exact c.dissipation_nonneg x hx'
```

